      "outputText": "Recommendation: a horizontally sharded WebSocket gateway tier fronting a stateless message-routing layer, with Kafka as the durable message backbone and ScyllaDB for message storage. Users connect over WebSocket to gateway nodes behind an L4 load balancer; at ~50–100k connections per node, 10M concurrent users needs roughly 150–250 gateway instances. Gateways are dumb pipes: they authenticate the connection (JWT), register the user's session location in a Redis cluster (user → gateway mapping), and forward inbound messages to Kafka topics partitioned by conversation ID. Stateless chat-service consumers process messages (persistence, fan-out logic, push notification triggers), write to ScyllaDB partitioned by conversation, and route deliveries: for online recipients, look up their gateway in Redis and publish to that gateway's pub/sub channel; for offline users, enqueue push notifications via APNs/FCM. Large group fan-out uses read-time fan-out (pull from the conversation partition) rather than write-time fan-out to avoid hot-key amplification.\n\nRun it all on Kubernetes across three availability zones with cell-based sharding (users assigned to cells of ~500k connections) so failures and deploys are blast-radius limited. Presence and typing indicators go through Redis pub/sub with TTL-based ephemeral state — never through Kafka or the database. Media (images, voice) is uploaded directly to object storage via presigned URLs, with only references flowing through the message path.\n\n- **Gateway/connections:** Go or Elixir WebSocket servers behind AWS NLB (L4)\n- **Message backbone:** Apache Kafka (partitioned by conversation ID)\n- **Message store:** ScyllaDB (Cassandra-compatible, low-latency at scale)\n- **Session/presence/routing:** Redis Cluster (session registry + pub/sub)\n- **Push notifications:** APNs / FCM via async workers\n- **Media:** S3 + CloudFront with presigned uploads\n- **Orchestration:** Kubernetes, multi-AZ, cell-based deployment\n- **Auth:** JWT with short-lived tokens, validated at the gateway\n- **Observability:** Prometheus + Grafana, OpenTelemetry tracing",
