      "outputText": "Run the chat plane as a stateless WebSocket edge tier fronted by anycast L4 load balancers: ~5,000 Go gateway pods at ~2,000 connections each (sized for headroom at 10M concurrent, with connections capped by memory, not CPU). Each gateway terminates TLS, authenticates a short-lived JWT, and registers the session in a Redis Cluster presence map (`user_id -> {gateway_id, device_id}`, TTL-refreshed by heartbeat). Gateways hold no durable state, so any pod can die without message loss. Message flow is write-first: a client send goes to the gateway, which produces to Kafka partitioned by `conversation_id`, guaranteeing per-conversation ordering. A fan-out service consumes those partitions, resolves recipients' gateway locations from Redis, and pushes over persistent gRPC streams between fan-out workers and gateways — avoiding the N² mesh of gateway-to-gateway routing. Persistence is a separate Kafka consumer writing to ScyllaDB with `(conversation_id, message_id)` as the primary key and Snowflake-style time-sortable IDs, giving cheap backward pagination and idempotent retries on client-supplied dedup keys.\n\nDeploy across three regions with users pinned to a home region by GeoDNS; cross-region traffic moves only through Kafka mirroring for conversations with participants in multiple regions, keeping the common case single-region. Offline delivery falls out of the same Kafka stream: a push worker consumes undelivered messages and hands them to APNs/FCM, while unread counters live in Redis with periodic ScyllaDB reconciliation. Large groups (>1,000 members) switch from per-recipient fan-out to a pull model where clients poll a cursor on reconnect, which caps the write amplification that otherwise kills broadcast channels. Capacity planning assumption: ~10 messages/user/minute peak, roughly 1.7M msg/s ingest — sustainable on ~200 Kafka partitions per topic set with 3× replication.\n\n- **Edge/transport:** Go + `gobwas/ws` (or `nbio`) WebSocket gateways, anycast + AWS NLB / Envoy, TLS 1.3\n- **Message bus:** Apache Kafka (KRaft mode), partitioned by `conversation_id`, cross-region MirrorMaker 2\n- **Presence & counters:** Redis Cluster, TTL heartbeats, Redis Streams for ephemeral typing indicators\n- **Message store:** ScyllaDB (Cassandra-compatible, no JVM GC pauses), TWCS compaction, S3 cold-tier archival\n- **Metadata/auth:** PostgreSQL (users, groups, device registry) with PgBouncer, JWT + refresh tokens\n- **Media:** direct-to-S3 presigned uploads, CloudFront CDN, out of the message path entirely\n- **Orchestration:** Kubernetes with HPA on connection count, Karpenter for node scaling\n- **Observability:** Prometheus + VictoriaMetrics for long retention, OpenTelemetry tracing, Grafana\n- **Protocol:** Protobuf over WebSocket frames, gRPC for internal service-to-service streams",
