      "messageSetId": "670c77a850bc355d3855766926b444ca63aa4e609d79dbde5a6b3e676e6f33a2",
      "outputText": "Recommendation: build a hybrid feed. Ordinary creators fan out on write into a bounded per-viewer inbox. Creators above a follower threshold skip fan-out, and their posts are pulled at read time from a per-author recent-posts list. A recommendation pipeline maintains a per-viewer candidate list. The feed service merges those three sources, runs every candidate through a batched authorization gate backed by the canonical post, graph, and account stores, ranks the survivors, and stores the ranked ids as a short-lived session snapshot so pages stay stable. Every page read, including later pages served from the snapshot, re-runs the gate on the ids it is about to return. Inboxes, recent lists, candidate lists, and snapshots only decide what is considered. The canonical stores decide what is shown.\n\nBoth guarantees come from write ordering. A post create commits to the post store, appends to the author's recent list, and enqueues one fan-out event before returning. A high-follower post is therefore eligible immediately, and an ordinary post is eligible as soon as workers push its id into follower inboxes, which is budgeted well inside the target. A delete, visibility change, block, or account privacy change commits to its canonical store, synchronously invalidates the affected keys in the visibility cache, and only then acknowledges. A failed invalidation means no acknowledgment. Since the gate consults that cache and falls back to the canonical store on a miss, no request that begins after the acknowledgment can pass stale data. Inbox and snapshot cleanup runs later in the background and is hygiene, not a correctness dependency.\n\n- **Canonical authorities**\n  - Post store, sharded by author id, for existence, content, per-post visibility, and deletion tombstones.\n  - Social graph store for follow edges, pending requests, blocks, and removed followers.\n  - Account settings store for account-level privacy.\n  - The visibility gate and its cache are derived and invalidated as part of acknowledgment, never authoritative. Inboxes, recent lists, candidate lists, and snapshots are rebuildable caches.\n\n- **Ownership keys**\n  - Posts keyed by time-ordered post id, partitioned by author id.\n  - Follow edges stored twice, by follower id for the read-time gate and by author id for fan-out.\n  - Inbox keyed by viewer id with a fixed length cap. Recent list keyed by author id, only for threshold-exceeding creators.\n  - Recommendation candidates keyed by viewer id. Snapshot keyed by viewer id plus session id with a short TTL.\n  - Visibility cache keyed by post id for post state, author id for account privacy, and viewer id for the viewer's follow set.\n  - Fan-out and invalidation topics partitioned by author id so one creator's events stay ordered.\n\n- **Bounded request paths**\n  - First page: read inbox, pull recent lists for followed high-follower creators, read candidates, dedupe, gate, rank, write snapshot, return. On timeout drop recommendations first, then the pull, never the gate.\n  - Later page: read the next snapshot slice, re-gate those ids, return. An expired snapshot triggers a fresh first-page build under the same caps.\n  - Post create: write post store, append recent list, enqueue one event, return. No per-follower work inline.\n  - Delete, visibility, block, unfollow, privacy change: commit canonical store, invalidate cache keys synchronously, publish cleanup event, then acknowledge.\n\n| Step | Cap |\n|---|---|\n| Inbox read | 500 ids |\n| High-follower pull | 100 creators, 20 posts each |\n| Candidate read | 200 ids |\n| Gate | one batched call per page |\n| Page size | 20 |\n| Page budget | 300 ms p99 |\n\n- **Background paths**\n  - Fan-out workers consume post events by author partition, skip threshold-exceeding creators, and push ids into inboxes under a p99 target inside the window.\n  - Cleanup workers consume invalidation events and lazily purge inboxes and snapshots.\n  - A classifier moves a creator to pull mode when their follower count crosses the threshold. Existing inbox entries stay valid.\n  - The recommendation pipeline refreshes candidate lists near-line and in batch.\n  - A reconciliation job samples inboxes against the post store and re-emits lost events.\n\n- **Permanent components**\n  - Post store, social graph store, account settings store, event log, visibility gate with cache, inbox store, recent-list store, candidate store, snapshot cache, feed service, ranking service.\n  - All exist at launch. The ranker starts as recency plus heuristics and recommendations start as graph-based trending, both behind fixed interfaces.\n\n- **Unknowns to settle**\n  - The fan-out threshold. Start near fifty thousand followers and tune on fan-out latency.\n  - Whether acknowledgment must hold across regions. If so, either serve the gate from one region or make acknowledgment wait for invalidation in every serving region.\n  - The maximum follows per viewer, which bounds the follow-set fetch inside the gate.\n  - Whether authors need read-your-writes on their own feed, since fan-out is asynchronous.",
