      "outputText": "Use a hybrid fan-out architecture with read-time authorization. On post creation, a write path publishes to a durable log (Kafka); a fan-out worker pushes post IDs into per-follower feed inboxes (Redis/ScyllaDB sorted sets, capped ~1,000 entries) for creators under a follower threshold (~50k), while posts from mega-creators are instead written only to a per-creator recent-posts index and merged at read time (fan-out-on-read). A feed request merges the viewer's precomputed inbox, the recent-post indexes of their followed mega-creators, and a batch of candidates from a recommendation service, then ranks them and hydrates content. Critically, the feed stores only IDs plus ranking features—never content or visibility state. Hydration at request time reads the post store and an authorization service that checks deletion tombstones and privacy/visibility rules synchronously; anything failing the check is filtered out before rendering and backfilled from the next-ranked candidates. This makes deletes and privacy changes take effect on the very next request after the source-of-truth write is acknowledged, without needing to purge millions of fanned-out inbox entries (those are cleaned lazily). The 30-second freshness bound is met because fan-out and index appends complete in seconds, and pagination uses cursor tokens (rank score + post ID) rather than offsets so pages stay stable as new items arrive.\n\nAt launch this runs as one small merge service, one fan-out worker pool, and modest Redis; at 10M DAU you scale by sharding inboxes by user ID, partitioning the log by creator ID, and adding a candidate cache for recommendations—no architectural change, only capacity.\n\n- **Canonical authorities:** post store (Postgres/ScyllaDB) for content and existence; social graph service for follow edges; authorization/visibility service for privacy state and tombstones; recommendation service for candidate scores. Feed inboxes and caches are derived, never authoritative.\n- **Ownership keys:** feed inbox keyed by `viewer_user_id`; recent-posts index keyed by `creator_id`; posts keyed by `post_id`; follow edges keyed by `(follower_id, followee_id)`; pagination cursor scoped to `(viewer_id, session_cursor)`.\n- **Bounded request path:** inbox read (capped list) + K mega-creator index reads (K bounded by followed mega-creators, capped) + one recommendation batch + one batched hydration/authz check per page (~30 items), all with per-page limits and timeouts.\n- **Bounded background path:** fan-out jobs bounded by follower count under the threshold; lazy inbox cleanup and cache invalidation on delete/privacy events consumed from the log; recommendation candidate precomputation on a schedule.\n- **Permanent components:** durable event log, post store, social graph, authorization service, feed-merge/ranking service, fan-out workers, inbox store, recommendation candidate generator. Caches and inboxes are rebuildable from the log and canonical stores.",
