      "outputText": "## Recommendation\n\nBuild a **hybrid fan-out timeline with read-time authorization**. Posts land in a canonical, sharded post store (shard by `post_id`, with a secondary author index by `creator_id`) and emit a durable change event. A fan-out worker pushes *post ID references only* into per-viewer timeline shards for creators below a follower threshold (~50k), while creators above it are marked **pull sources**: their posts are never fanned out, and each read merges the follower's small pull-source list at query time. This keeps write amplification bounded — no post ever costs 10M writes — and keeps the 30s eligibility budget achievable (target p99 fan-out completion ≤ 10s via chunked, parallel follower-range jobs). The timeline entry is a *hint*, never a truth claim: it carries `(post_id, creator_id, timestamp, ranking features)` and nothing renderable.\n\nCorrectness under deletion and privacy change comes from making the **hydration step the only place content becomes visible**. Every feed request hydrates candidate IDs through a filter that checks the canonical post record and the visibility service for the specific viewer; anything deleted, restricted, blocked, or newly private is dropped and back-filled from the next candidates. Deletes and privacy changes write to the canonical store and *synchronously invalidate the hydration cache before acknowledging* — cache entries are keyed `(post_id, visibility_version)`, so a version bump makes every stale copy unaddressable rather than merely expiring. Timeline shards are cleaned lazily in the background; they are allowed to be wrong because they are never served directly. Ranking is a bounded re-scoring pass over a fixed candidate set: ~600 followed candidates + ~400 recommendation candidates from a separate retrieval service, scored by one model call, diversified, then paged with an opaque cursor carrying `(score, post_id, visibility_version)` for stable pagination.\n\n**Canonical authorities**\n- Post store — sole authority for post content, existence, and current privacy setting.\n- Visibility service — sole authority for viewer↔content permission (follows, blocks, private accounts, audience lists); every hydration consults it.\n- Follow graph service — sole authority for edges and follower counts; owns the pull-source designation.\n- Ranking/recommendation service — authority for scores only, never for eligibility.\n- Timeline store — authority for *nothing*; a rebuildable, best-effort index of candidate IDs.\n\n**Ownership keys**\n- `post_id` — post record, tombstone, visibility_version.\n- `creator_id` — author post index, pull-source flag, follower bucket ranges.\n- `viewer_id` — timeline shard, seen/impression set, feed cursor state.\n- `(follower_id, creator_id)` — the follow edge; reverse index bucketed as `(creator_id, bucket_no)`.\n- `(post_id, visibility_version)` — hydration cache entry.\n- `(viewer_id, post_id)` — dedupe and impression suppression.\n\n**Bounded request path** (hard ceilings, no unbounded work)\n- Merge ≤ 200 pull-source creators × ≤ 20 recent posts each, from a per-creator cache.\n- Read ≤ 1,000 timeline entries from one viewer shard.\n- One retrieval call for ≤ 400 recommendation candidates, with timeout and empty-on-failure degradation.\n- One batched hydration + authorization call over ≤ 1,000 IDs; over-fetch by ~30% to absorb filtered drops.\n- One ranking pass, fixed page size (≤ 25), total budget ~150ms p99; every dependency has a timeout and a defined degraded result.\n\n**Bounded background path**\n- Fan-out jobs chunked by follower bucket (≤ 10k writes per job), parallel, resumable from checkpoint, idempotent by `(viewer_id, post_id)`.\n- Timeline trimming to a fixed cap (~2,000 entries) per viewer.\n- Lazy tombstone sweep and follower-count reclassification into/out of pull-source status.\n- Backfill on follow, unfollow removal, and periodic timeline rebuild from the author index — the rebuild path is what makes the timeline store disposable.\n\n**Permanent components** (survive every scale rewrite)\n- Canonical post store and its immutable tombstone log.\n- Visibility/authorization service with the synchronous pre-ack invalidation contract.\n- Follow graph with the hybrid push/pull threshold.\n- The ID-only timeline index plus its fan-out pipeline and rebuild job.\n- Hydration-and-filter layer as the single rendering gate.\n- Candidate generation, ranking, and the opaque pagination cursor.\n- Seen/impression store.",
