      "outputText": "Use a hybrid fan-out architecture. A durable post-event log feeds a recent-post index and per-viewer timeline KV store: ordinary creators fan out to followers asynchronously, while high-follower creators are read from an author-partitioned pull index at request time. Feed requests merge bounded candidates from the viewer timeline, followed-author pull indexes, and recommendation services, then rank them with a cursor containing ranking/version and time boundaries. Events are processed with an SLA that makes posts eligible within 30 seconds.\n\nTreat post visibility, deletion, and privacy policy as authoritative in a policy service backed by a durable revocation/tombstone ledger. Every candidate is policy-checked in batches, and content delivery performs a final authorization check; a deletion or privacy event invalidates cached/materialized entries and advances the affected post’s policy version, so later requests cannot return it even if stale timeline rows remain.\n\n- **Canonical authorities:** identity and follows → account/graph service; post content and metadata → post service; visibility/deletion/privacy → policy service plus durable tombstone ledger; ranking → versioned ranking service.\n- **Ownership keys:** `user_id` owns personal timeline partitions; `author_id` owns post and pull-index partitions; `post_id` owns content, policy version, and tombstone state; recommendation data is keyed by model/version and viewer segment.\n- **Bounded request paths:** authenticate viewer, read a fixed candidate budget from timeline KV, followed-author pull indexes, and recommendations, batch policy-check candidates, rank, hydrate, and final-check authorization before returning a cursor page.\n- **Bounded background paths:** post events update the pull index and fan out only to capped ordinary-author follower sets; celebrity posts remain pull-based; privacy/deletion events publish invalidations to caches, timelines, search/index stores, and downstream consumers.\n- **Permanent components:** durable event log, post/blob store, follow-graph store, author recent-post indexes, viewer timeline KV, recommendation candidate store, ranker, policy/tombstone ledger, invalidation bus, caches, observability and replay tooling.",
