      "outputText": "Use stateless HTTP app replicas with one replicated, disk-backed Valkey cluster sharded from day one. Posts, deletion state, and privacy ACLs are owned by `creator_id`; follows, user features, and feed cursors by `user_id`. New posts synchronously enter the creator’s recent-post index, while bounded recommendation indexes are updated through retry-safe BullMQ jobs in the same Valkey plane. Feed requests merge a fixed-size candidate set of recent followed posts and recommendations, rank it in the app, and recheck every item’s current ACL/deletion state on the authoritative creator shard before returning it. ACL reads use the shard leader or a replica known to have applied the acknowledged mutation, so acknowledged deletion or privacy changes cannot be hidden by stale feed candidates.\n\n- **Canonical authority:** Replicated, persistent Valkey; post content metadata, ACLs, deletion status, and recent-post indexes are authoritative. Recommendation indexes are derived and rebuildable.\n- **Ownership keys:** `creator_id` for posts and visibility; `user_id` for follows, preferences, features, and cursors; `bucket_id` for derived recommendation indexes. Never fan out a post to all followers.\n- **Bounded request path:** Read one bounded follow slice, up to configured limits of followed-post and recommendation candidates, fetch their metadata, rank, ACL-filter, and return a cursor. Candidate count, page size, and follow slice limits must be fixed and load-tested; their numeric values are currently unknown.\n- **Bounded background path:** Owner-partitioned BullMQ jobs update recommendation buckets with deterministic post-based IDs, retries, backpressure, and rebuild-from-authority recovery. The indexing path has a 30-second completion target.\n- **Permanent components:** Stateless app replicas, Valkey shards with replicas and persistence, and BullMQ execution inside those app replicas. No separate feed service, Kafka stream, per-follower materialized feed, cache, CQRS projection, or placement service.\n- **Revisit trigger:** If the product requires considering an unbounded follow set or candidate pool per request, or if measured post/index volume exceeds shard capacity, the bounded contract must be revisited; 10 million daily users alone does not establish capacity.",
