      "outputText": "Use a hybrid fan-out architecture. Store posts and privacy state in a strongly consistent Post/Policy service, emit post, follow, deletion, and privacy events through a durable log, and maintain per-viewer inboxes for ordinary creators plus per-creator candidate indexes for high-fanout creators. A feed request merges recent followed-post candidates, recommendation candidates, and high-fanout creator candidates, then ranks them using a stateless ranking service. New-post events must update eligibility indexes and caches within 30 seconds; deletes and privacy changes synchronously advance a content-policy version and publish invalidation events.\n\nEvery feed read performs an authoritative policy check—or validates against a policy snapshot whose version is at least the viewer’s required invalidation watermark—before returning content. Deleted or newly unauthorized content is filtered even if it remains in an inbox, ranking cache, CDN response, or recommendation index. The design assumes durable event delivery, bounded staleness for ranking, and explicitly preserves the product choice still unknown: whether “within 30 seconds” is a typical or hard availability SLO.\n\n- Canonical authorities: Post/Policy service for content and authorization; Follow graph service for relationships; durable event log for ordered changes; ranking service for scores.\n- Ownership keys: `post_id` owns post state and policy version; `creator_id` owns creator candidate indexes and high-fanout streams; `viewer_id` owns personalized inboxes; `viewer_id + feed_generation` owns request snapshots.\n- Bounded request paths: read at most fixed candidate counts per source; merge, rank, policy-filter, and paginate with a bounded deadline; never synchronously traverse all followed creators or all creator followers.\n- Bounded background paths: event consumers process fixed-size batches with retries and dead-letter queues; fan out only to bounded follower cohorts; high-fanout creators use pull-based indexing; invalidation propagates by `post_id` and policy version.\n- Permanent components: strongly consistent Post/Policy store, Follow graph, durable event log, inbox/candidate stores, recommendation store, ranking service, policy-version/invalidation service, feed API, cache layer, observability and replay tooling.",
