      "outputText": "Use one stateless HTTP deployable backed by a sharded, replicated, disk-backed Redis/Valkey authority. Shard by `viewer_id` for personalized state and by `creator_id` for creator post streams, using stable hash tags and replicas for hot creator reads. On each request, bounded fan-in reads the viewer’s followed-creator streams plus recommendation candidates, ranks the resulting capped set, and rechecks current post visibility before returning it. Publishing a post atomically inserts it into the creator stream, making it eligible immediately; deletion or privacy changes atomically update the authoritative visibility record, and every later feed request filters against that record, so stale candidate indexes cannot expose content.\n\n- Canonical authority: sharded replicated disk-backed Redis/Valkey containing follows, creator recent-post streams, recommendation candidates, post metadata, visibility state, tombstones, and per-viewer cursors.\n- Ownership keys: `viewer_id` for follows, feed cursors, and personalization; `creator_id` for post streams; visibility is owned by the post’s creator shard or stable `post_id` owner.\n- Bounded request path: read at most a fixed number of recent posts per followed-creator batch and recommendation candidates, merge/rank in the app replica, then perform authoritative visibility checks before response.\n- Bounded background path: optional retry-safe recommendation refresh and stream maintenance in ordinary app replicas using owner-partitioned jobs; no follower fan-out queue.\n- Permanent components: stateless HTTP app replicas, sharded replicated Redis/Valkey authority, and ordinary app-replica background execution.\n- Capacity scaling: add Redis/Valkey shards and replicas while preserving the same ownership and request contract; celebrity creators use replicated creator-stream reads rather than per-follower materialized feeds.\n- Revisit triggers: measured viewer follow counts or candidate fan-in exceed the request bound, a single creator shard becomes a sustained hot-spot, or recommendation freshness requires a separately measured compute pipeline.",
