      "outputText": "Use a hybrid push/pull feed. A transactional post service writes each post and its visibility policy, then emits a durable `PostPublished` event. For creators below a capacity-based fanout threshold, workers append post IDs to viewer-owned inbox shards; for high-fanout creators, posts remain in a creator-owned recent outbox and are pulled only for followers at request time. A recommendation pipeline consumes the same events and maintains bounded per-user/topic candidate indexes. Each request merges fixed-size windows—such as 400 followed candidates, 200 hot-creator candidates, and 400 recommendations—ranks them, and returns a page with opaque source cursors. Event consumers and the recent-post index have a 30-second eligibility SLO.\n\nDeletion and privacy changes are committed to the canonical visibility authority, with a new policy version or tombstone, before the mutation is acknowledged. Every feed request batch-checks current visibility and follow authorization using a strongly consistent policy gate before fetching content; stale inboxes, outboxes, recommendation indexes, and caches therefore cannot expose unauthorized posts. Asynchronous purge workers remove invalid IDs for hygiene, but never provide the security guarantee.\n\n- **Canonical authorities:** Post/content and visibility service keyed by `PostID`; follow graph keyed by `(ViewerID, CreatorID)`; durable event log for propagation only. Derived feed stores are never authoritative.\n- **Ownership keys:** User inbox by `(ViewerID, lane, time bucket)`; creator outbox by `(CreatorID, time bucket)`; recommendation candidates by `(ViewerID, source)`; policy/tombstone state by `PostID` and `VisibilityVersion`.\n- **Bounded request path:** Read fixed candidate caps from each source, batch-fetch metadata/features, batch-authorize before content retrieval, rank, and paginate with opaque cursors. Never enumerate all followers or scan an unbounded feed.\n- **Bounded background path:** Publish one durable event; fan out only to bounded-follower creators in chunked, idempotent batches; use pull for hot creators; update recommendation indexes within 30 seconds; process deletion/privacy tombstones asynchronously with retries and dead-letter handling.\n- **Permanent components:** Post store, visibility/authorization store, follow-graph store, event log, creator outboxes, user inbox shards, recommendation candidate index, feature store, ranker, authorization gate, content cache, and purge/observability workers.",
