      "outputText": "Use a hybrid push/pull feed. Store posts, visibility state, account privacy, and follow edges in a strongly consistent distributed SQL database. Publishing atomically creates the post and its ordered author-outbox entry; CDC emits the change to Kafka. Fanout workers push opaque post IDs for creators below 100,000 followers into bounded per-viewer inboxes, while larger creators remain pull-on-read. Recommendations are written as separate per-viewer candidate lists. Each request merges inbox IDs, recommendations, and recent author-outbox heads for followed creators, then ranks them. A product limit of 5,000 follows keeps the pull path bounded, and the recent-head overlay makes a committed post eligible within 30 seconds even when fanout is delayed.\n\nCandidate stores are never authorization authorities. After ranking—and again on every paginated request—an authorization-and-hydration gateway batch-checks the top IDs using a linearizable read of current post status, ACL version, creator privacy, blocks, and follow relationships. Deletion or privacy mutation increments a visibility version or writes a tombstone; acknowledgment is returned only after that transaction commits. The gateway then omits unauthorized posts and only mints short-lived media URLs for the surviving versions. Stale inboxes, recommendation lists, caches, and cursors are therefore harmless; authorization failure fails closed.\n\n- **Canonical authorities:** distributed SQL for posts/tombstones, visibility and account privacy, and follow/block edges; immutable object storage for media bytes, with the database remaining authoritative for access.\n- **Ownership keys:** `post_id` for post visibility; `creator_id` for account policy and author outboxes; `(creator_id, follower_id)` for relationship edges; `viewer_id` for inboxes, recommendation lists, pagination state, and ranking features.\n- **Bounded paths:** request path reads at most 400 inbox IDs, 200 recommendation IDs, and one batched recent-head record per followed creator, ranks at most 5,600 candidates, and strongly authorizes/hydrates at most 50 results; fanout jobs process follower ranges in 1,000-edge idempotent chunks, inboxes retain 2,000 IDs, and retries use capped queues plus dead-letter storage.\n- **Permanent components:** API gateway, content/follow authority, transactional outbox and Kafka, author-outbox cache, fanout workers, sharded feed store, recommendation pipeline, ranker, authorization/hydration gateway, object storage/CDN, replay tooling, metrics, tracing, and audit logs. Shard counts and the 100,000-follower threshold should be tuned from still-unknown peak request, publishing, and follower-distribution measurements without changing this topology.",
