      "outputText": "Use pull-on-read with no follower fanout. Run a stateless HTTP feed/ranking module over one replicated, disk-backed, no-eviction Valkey cluster sharded from day one. Publishing atomically stores the post’s current visibility state, appends it to the creator’s recent-post log, and records an outbox entry. App replicas lease outbox batches and idempotently add eligible posts to at most `K` topic recommendation logs within 30 seconds. A creator with millions of followers therefore still causes `O(K)` writes, not millions.\n\nEach feed request reads the viewer’s follows and interests, pipelines creator-log heads plus bounded refills, merges a bounded recommendation sample, ranks at most `C` candidates, and keyset-paginates them. Immediately before returning a page, it reads every selected post’s current authoritative state and evaluates privacy against the current follow edge; deletion/privacy acknowledgements occur only after a durable commit. Stale feed references can cause omissions but cannot disclose content. `F`, `K`, and `C` are enforced limits whose values require the missing peak-RPS, posting-rate, and follows-per-viewer measurements; 10 million DAU alone does not prove capacity.\n\n- **Canonical authorities:** Non-expiring post/tombstone/privacy heads and creator timelines; current viewer follow edges and interest profiles. Recommendation logs are rebuildable derived indexes.\n- **Ownership keys:** `creator_id` for posts and creator timelines, `viewer_id` for follows, and `(topic_id, stripe_id)` for recommendation logs, routed through fixed virtual shards.\n- **Bounded request path:** At most `F` followed-creator heads, `C` total refills/recommendations, and `C` authoritative visibility checks; exhaustion returns a shorter page rather than scanning indefinitely.\n- **Bounded background path:** One durable outbox record per publication and no more than `K` idempotent recommendation-index writes; no per-follower work.\n- **Permanent components:** `client → stateless app replicas → Valkey shards`, with the same app replicas processing Valkey outboxes. Launch and 10-million-DAU topology differ only in replica, shard, and partition-assignment counts.",
