      "outputText": "Use a hybrid fan-out architecture. Posts and relationship/privacy changes are committed to a strongly consistent metadata store, then published through a durable partitioned log. A feed materializer writes post IDs into per-user inboxes for ordinary creators, while posts from high-fan-out creators and recommendation candidates are merged at read time. Feed requests fetch bounded candidate sets from the inbox, followed-creator outboxes, and recommendation service; a stateless ranker scores them, hydrates selected posts from a content cache/store, and returns an opaque cursor containing ranking-version, time boundary, and tie-breaker. Creator thresholds can change dynamically without changing correctness, and log lag is monitored so new posts become candidates within the 30-second SLO.\n\nDeletion and privacy correctness is enforced on the serving path, not entrusted to asynchronous fan-out cleanup. Once a mutation is acknowledged, the authoritative post/visibility record and a compact deny/tombstone index have committed before acknowledgment. Every hydrated candidate is batch-authorized against that current authority (or a coherently invalidated versioned cache); failures are omitted. Cleanup workers subsequently remove stale IDs from inboxes, outboxes, caches, search/recommendation indexes, and media storage, but those systems never determine visibility.\n\n- **Canonical authorities:** strongly consistent post metadata/visibility store; follower and block graph store; account/privacy policy store; media object store for bytes, referenced only after authorization. The durable event log is the ordering/replay backbone, not the final authority.\n- **Ownership keys:** posts/outboxes/log partitions by `creator_id`; home inboxes and pagination state by `viewer_id`; relationship records by `(viewer_id, creator_id)`; tombstones and content-cache entries by `post_id`; recommendation features by `entity_id` with versioned snapshots.\n- **Bounded request paths:** one bounded batch from the viewer inbox, bounded top-K reads from only high-fan-out followed outboxes selected via an indexed follow graph, one bounded recommendation batch, rank top-K, batch hydrate, then batch-authorize every result. No request scans all followers, all follows, or unbounded history.\n- **Bounded background paths:** ordinary fan-out is chunked into idempotent follower batches with checkpoints, retries, and dead-letter handling; celebrity posts skip follower-wide fan-out; deletion/privacy events synchronously establish denial, then trigger rate-limited asynchronous cleanup; compaction, backfills, and threshold migrations operate from replayable logs with quotas.\n- **Permanent components:** API gateway and feed service; post/relationship/privacy services; strongly consistent metadata and graph databases; partitioned event log; per-user inbox store; per-creator outbox store; recommendation candidate service; stateless ranking service; authorization/visibility service with versioned cache; content/media cache and object storage; idempotent materializers and cleanup workers; schema registry, observability, SLO alerts, audit log, replay tooling, and multi-region disaster recovery.",
