      "outputText": "Build a hybrid, ID-only feed using stateless HTTP/app replicas and one no-eviction, disk-backed, replicated Valkey cluster, sharded from launch by stable owner keys. Publishing atomically writes the creator-owned post, a non-expiring visibility/deletion head, a bounded recent-post log, and a delivery manifest. Replicas lease bounded manifest batches and idempotently append references to viewer home logs. A creator uses fanout-on-write only when measured capacity proves its current audience can be delivered within 30 seconds; otherwise it is pull-on-read, so a celebrity post is immediately eligible from its creator log without millions of recipient writes. Recommendation generation uses the same lease loop to maintain a bounded, viewer-owned list of post IDs.\n\nFor each page, rank a fixed overscan of inbox and recommendation IDs plus a fixed recent window from pull-only follows, then hydrate only after current viewer-entitlement and creator-owned visibility checks; candidates never contain renderable post data. A deletion or privacy change advances an unexpired monotonic tombstone/version before acknowledgement, with durable replica/failover confirmation; failed or stale authorization checks omit the item, so delayed fanout and cleanup cannot leak it. Launch and 10 million DAU use the same graph, adding only shards, read replicas, and app replicas. Maximum follows, page latency, retention, and ranking freshness remain unspecified; they set the fixed budgets, and exact ranking over an unbounded follow set is not capacity-proven.\n\n- **Canonical authorities:** Creator-shard posts and visibility/tombstone heads; viewer-shard follow and entitlement state. Feed inboxes, recommendations, recent indexes, follower delivery indexes, and manifests are derived structures in the same cluster.\n\n- **Ownership keys:** `creator_id` owns posts, privacy state, recent logs, and delivery manifests; `viewer_id` owns follows, entitlements, inboxes, and recommendation lists. Delivery is idempotent on `(post_id, viewer_id)`.\n\n- **Bounded paths:** A page uses fixed candidate, recommendation, and per-source recent windows; leased fanout uses fixed recipient batches and switches to pull when it cannot meet 30 seconds. Cleanup is best-effort and never authorizes content.\n\n- **Permanent components:** Stateless app replicas, including lease handlers, and the replicated sharded Valkey authority. No separate feed service, broker, dedicated worker fleet, or response cache is required.",
