      "outputText": "Use a hybrid fanout feed. Store posts and visibility policy durably, then publish each new-post event to a stream. For normal creators, asynchronously fan out post references into follower inbox shards; for high-follower creators, keep posts in a creator outbox and merge them at read time. A feed request reads the user’s inbox plus followed-creator outboxes and recommendation candidates, ranks a bounded candidate set, and returns a cursor derived from the ranking snapshot. This supports new-post eligibility well within 30 seconds while avoiding write amplification for celebrity creators.\n\nMake visibility enforcement authoritative at read time: every candidate carries its post/version and visibility state, and the feed service filters against the current policy before returning it. Deletion/privacy acknowledgements synchronously update the canonical visibility record and invalidate/mark affected cached entries; asynchronous inbox cleanup is only an optimization. Thus no later request can reveal content after acknowledgement, even if stale fanout data remains.\n\n- **Canonical authorities**\n  - Post service: post body, deletion status, post version.\n  - Social graph service: follow edges and block/mute relationships.\n  - Privacy/authorization service: viewer eligibility policy and policy version.\n  - Feed service: inbox references, cursors, and ranking snapshots—not content visibility truth.\n  - Recommendation service: candidate generation and model/version metadata.\n\n- **Ownership keys**\n  - Posts and creator outboxes: `creator_id`, partitioned by time.\n  - Follow graph: `follower_id` for reads; reverse `creator_id` index for fanout.\n  - Feed inbox: `viewer_id` with shard/bucket suffix.\n  - Visibility cache/invalidation: `post_id` and policy version.\n  - Recommendation state: `viewer_id`.\n\n- **Bounded request/background paths**\n  - Request path: fetch a capped number of inbox/outbox/recommendation candidates, authorize/filter, rank, and paginate.\n  - Publish path: durable event → normal-creator inbox fanout or celebrity outbox append.\n  - Cleanup path: asynchronously remove deleted/private post references from inboxes and caches.\n  - Privacy/delete path: synchronously commit canonical policy/status before acknowledgement; publish invalidations and cleanup work afterward.\n\n- **Permanent components**\n  - Durable post store and media service.\n  - Social graph store.\n  - Privacy/authorization store with low-latency read replicas.\n  - Event log/stream and idempotent consumers.\n  - Sharded feed-inbox store and creator-outbox store.\n  - Candidate/ranking service with feature store.\n  - Cache layer, invalidation service, observability, replay/backfill tooling, and abuse/rate-limit controls.",
