      "outputText": "Use a pull-ranked feed: stateless feed replicas read the viewer’s follow edges, fetch bounded recent candidate IDs from per-creator append-only post logs, merge them with a viewer-partitioned recommendation index, then rank and paginate with opaque cursors. Posts are appended synchronously to their creator shard and are therefore eligible on the next feed read; active clients poll every few seconds, so the 30-second eligibility target needs no fanout-to-millions-of-followers job. Every returned candidate is rechecked against the canonical post visibility/deletion state before response, so an acknowledged deletion or privacy change immediately suppresses it even if it remains in a derived candidate log. Capacity grows by adding replicas and reassigning owner shards; the same topology serves launch and 10M DAU.\n\n- **Canonical authorities:** replicated disk-backed post/visibility authority (creator-owned); follow graph and recommendation candidates (viewer-owned). Derived creator candidate logs and recommendation indexes may be stale, but never authorize display.\n- **Ownership keys:** posts and privacy state by `creator_id`; follows, feed cursors, recommendation candidates, and feed-rate limits by `viewer_id`. A post ID resolves to its creator shard.\n- **Bounded request path:** one viewer shard supplies a bounded page of follows and recommendations; fetch only a fixed recent window per followed creator, enforce the product’s maximum active-follow set or request budget, rank a fixed candidate cap, and canonical-visibility-check only the selected results. The required follow-set/page/candidate limits are currently unknown and must be specified; without them, per-request capacity is unproven.\n- **Bounded background path:** append each new post once to its creator log; asynchronously update viewer-owned recommendation candidates in idempotent, bounded batches. Do not fan out followed posts to every follower, especially for celebrity creators.\n- **Permanent components:** horizontally replicated feed/app deployable; one sharded, replicated durable authority with creator- and viewer-partitioned tables/keyspaces; bounded polling HTTP API. No separate feed service, broker, cache authority, websocket fleet, or celebrity-specific topology is required.",
