      "outputText": "Use a hybrid fanout feed. Publishing atomically commits a versioned post and its visibility state, appends a durable outbox event, and writes the creator’s recent-post log. Normal creators fan out lightweight post references into follower inboxes; creators with ≥100k followers instead fan out one coalesced “active creator” marker per follower per five-minute window, while readers pull the bounded recent posts from that creator’s log. Priority delivery targets the inbox/marker path within 30 seconds. A feed request reads a fixed candidate budget (for example, 1,500 inbox refs, 100 active-creator markers × five posts, and 500 recommendation refs), ranks them, then batch-hydrates only enough results to return a 50-item page.\n\nDeletion and privacy changes are correctness-critical: acknowledge them only after a linearizable update to the post/creator visibility authority. Every feed response—including paginated results and cache hits—passes selected post IDs through a strongly consistent authorization gate before content or media URLs are returned. Fanout cleanup, cache invalidation, and recommendation-index removal run asynchronously; stale references are harmless because they contain no content and cannot pass the final gate. The threshold and budgets are operational knobs, not correctness assumptions.\n\n- **Canonical authorities:** versioned Post Ledger for existence/deletion; Privacy and Relationship Graph for current audience eligibility; Follow Graph for edges; Author Timeline for recent post references. Feed inboxes, recommendation indexes, and caches are derived only.\n\n- **Ownership keys:** `postId` owns post state; `creatorId` owns timeline and audience epoch; `viewerId` owns inbox, active-creator markers, and feed cursor state; follow edges are canonically owned by `followerId`, with a versioned reverse projection by `creatorId` for delivery.\n\n- **Bounded request/background paths:** request path is fixed-budget candidate reads, ranking, and bounded batch authorization/hydration; it never scans a follower list. Background paths are idempotent outbox consumers for fanout, coalesced marker delivery, recommendation indexing, tombstones, and cache cleanup, partitioned by destination `viewerId` and replayable from the durable log.\n\n- **Permanent components:** strongly consistent Post Ledger and authorization gate; versioned Follow/Privacy Graph; durable outbox/event log with replay and dead-letter handling; sharded author timelines and viewer inboxes; fanout/marker workers; candidate generation and ranking service; content/media service that requires authorization on every feed hydration.",
