      "outputText": "Use a hybrid timeline in one stateless feed application backed by a replicated, disk-persistent sharded Valkey/Redis authority. Publishing atomically writes the post, its current visibility/deletion head, its creator’s recent-post log, and deterministic fanout work. Posts from ordinary creators fan out as opaque references into follower inboxes; posts from creators above a measured follower threshold never fan out and are merged from the creator’s recent-post log at read time. A page ranks a fixed candidate set from the recipient inbox, followed high-follower creators, and per-user recommendation references; it hydrates and returns an item only after checking the current post visibility and viewer relationship. Deletion or privacy acknowledgement is the atomic visibility-head update, so stale inbox and recommendation references can be cleaned up asynchronously without ever being served.\n\nDay one and 10 million daily users use this same graph; capacity grows only by adding Valkey partitions and application replicas. The 30-second requirement is met by a bounded ordinary-creator fanout deadline and immediate pull eligibility for high-follower creators. Actual post rate, follow-count distribution, page-size/latency target, and recommendation freshness are unknown, so the product must set and enforce the ordinary-creator threshold, maximum followed high-follower creators examined per page, and candidate-page bounds; unlimited follows combined with a requirement to consider every followed creator on every page would invalidate this bounded request shape.\n\n- **Canonical authorities:** creator-sharded post/visibility heads and recent-post logs; viewer-sharded following state, inbox reference sets, and recommendation reference sets. Reverse follower indexes and fanout work records are derived, recoverable data in the same authority.\n- **Ownership keys:** `{creatorId}` for posts, privacy state, recent logs, and ordinary-creator fanout work; `{viewerId}` for follows, inboxes, recommendations, and idempotent feed-reference insertion.\n- **Bounded paths:** request reads fixed-size candidate batches, checks visibility in batch, and ranks a fixed maximum; background app modules lease deterministic post fanout batches and per-viewer recommendation refresh work. Duplicate fanout is harmless because each inbox uses post ID as its member key.\n- **Permanent components:** horizontally replicated feed/application replicas, including leased-job handlers, plus the sharded replicated Valkey/Redis authority. No separate feed service, broker, cache, projection store, or dedicated worker deployment is retained.",
