      "outputText": "Use one horizontally replicated stateless HTTP application and one replicated, disk-backed database with strongly consistent reads and transactions, partitioned by owner from launch. Generate feeds on read: retrieve bounded samples from followed creators’ recent-post indexes and topic-matched public-post indexes, then rank the combined candidates using recency and viewer interests. Publishing atomically writes the post and its creator-owned discovery indexes, making it eligible immediately upon acknowledgment—within the 30-second requirement. Rotate candidate sources across pages; eligibility means participation in retrieval, not guaranteed appearance. A creator with millions of followers still performs one publication transaction, without copying posts to followers.\n\nBefore returning any content, batch-read authoritative post status, creator privacy, and viewer access grants for shortlisted candidates. These checks must observe acknowledged mutations; unavailable checks exclude the affected content. Apply the same authorization to media access. Day 1 and 10 million daily users use the same request flow and component types, growing application replicas and database shards. Daily users alone cannot establish capacity: peak request rate, follow-count distribution, post volume, ranking-quality targets, and hottest-creator traffic remain unknown.\n\n- **Canonical authorities and ownership keys:** Creator-owned posts, visibility, access grants, and transactional discovery indexes use `creator_id`. Viewer-owned follow subscriptions and ranking preferences use `viewer_id`. Following expresses feed interest; the creator-owned grant determines private-content access. Discovery indexes never confer authorization.\n- **Bounded request path:** As initial engineering budgets, probe at most 24 followed creators and 8 recommendation shard indexes, retrieve at most 512 candidates, authorize at most 64 shortlisted posts, and return up to 20 items. Use bounded indexed reads and an opaque pagination cursor carrying traversal state. No request scans every followee, follower, or shard. These budgets require quality and latency validation; they are not measured capacity claims.\n- **Background path:** None is required for publication eligibility or feed generation. Publication, deletion, privacy changes, and grants are synchronous owner-local transactions. Optional future ranking enrichment cannot delay eligibility or become an authorization authority.\n- **Permanent components and their rent:** The application performs retrieval, ranking, and authorization; the database supplies durable ownership, transactional indexes, and current permissions. Both remain necessary when the design is collapsed. No separate feed service, broker, worker fleet, cache, or recommendation datastore is justified by the supplied requirements.\n- **Three failures and corrections:** Stale candidates are filtered by current authorization, with no permissive fallback. Ambiguous publication outcomes converge through an owner-local deterministic request ID. Celebrity reads or excessive sampling can break latency or ranking quality: test peak traffic, owner skew, and retrieval recall against targets fixed beforehand. If one creator exceeds one owner shard’s capacity, or bounded sampling cannot meet required recall, revisit that specific constraint before claiming the design meets the full envelope.",
